HISTORY_VERSION 1.0.0

TYPE Governance

STATUS APPROVED

DATE 2026-07-25

TITLE

Documentation Standard added: AIs create documentation and presentations
in ClickUp when the ROOT_AUTHORITY wants it.

WHY

The President directed that PACE's structure must itself indicate that an
AI, when the user wants it, creates documentation and presentations in
ClickUp rather than as scattered local files or content trapped in a chat.
This is a standing preference of authority applying across all governed
projects — an ORGANIZATION-scope rule under the Learning Protocol.

DECISION

Logged the observation as REQUEST-0003 (SCOPE ORGANIZATION) and promoted
it to standards/DOCUMENTATION_STANDARD_0.1.0.pdl. The standard is opt-in
(the AI acts on request or a standing instruction, not on its own),
places documentation as a ClickUp Doc inside the project's folder and
presentations as a deck-structured Doc, and keeps .pace/ as the memory of
record while ClickUp is the editable presentation surface.

IMPACT

The third pass through the Knowledge Intake loop in a single session. PACE
now carries an explicit, citable rule for where produced documents live,
complementing the Project-Management Standard for how work is tracked.

NEXT_STEPS

When the Bootstrap/Handoff engine is built, this rule loads automatically
so an AI already knows to offer/produce ClickUp Docs without being
reminded. Wire ClickUp Doc creation into the relevant engine once handoff
exists.

APPROVED_BY

President Cley Duarte

END
